<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Habsburg-Laufenburg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1232–1408</span> · Also known as House of Habsburg-Laufenburg</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Habsburg-Laufenburg was a junior line of the House of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a>, founded when the Habsburg lands were divided between brothers around 1232. Its counts held Laufenburg on the Upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a>, the landgraviate of the Klettgau and, for a time, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rapperswil">Rapperswil</a>. The line died out in 1408, and the Klettgau passed by marriage to the counts of Sulz.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/habsburg-laufenburg.jpg" alt="Habsburg-Laufenburg" width="320" height="436" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Napoleon Vier at Dutch Wikipedia · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Habsburgenses.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
